<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Szeged</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Szeged is the largest city of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tisza">Tisza</a> River near the Serbian and Romanian borders. A medieval royal town and then an Ottoman garrison from 1543 to 1686, it was almost destroyed by the great flood of 1879 and rebuilt to a planned design with ring boulevards. Its university and its paprika and salami industries made it a regional centre.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/szeged.jpg" alt="Szeged" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Szilas · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ferenc_M%C3%B3ra_Museum_2021-03-02,_Szeged.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
